---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const tMobileServiceUrl = "https://www.t-mobile.com/coverage/satellite-phone-service";
const tMobileChooseServiceUrl = "https://www.t-mobile.com/coverage/satellite-phone-service/choose-your-satellite-service";
const tMobileTrialUrl = "https://secure.t-mobile.com/network";
const tMobileEligibilityUrl = "https://www.t-mobile.com/resources/bring-your-own-phone#phone-check";
const tMobileSupportUrl = "https://www.t-mobile.com/support/coverage/satellite-support";
const tMobileAppsUrl = `${tMobileSupportUrl}#apps`;
const tMobileText911Url = "https://www.t-mobile.com/coverage/satellite-phone-service/standalone-sign-up?planId=TSAT911";
const appleSatelliteUrl = "https://support.apple.com/en-us/101573";
const pixelSatelliteUrl = "https://support.google.com/pixelphone/answer/15254448?hl=en";
const checkedDate = "August 8, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Get satellite service"
  description="T-Mobile T-Satellite options for using apps over limited satellite connections, including phone and plan requirements."
>
  <article class="info-page">
    <header class="info-hero">
      <h1>Get satellite service</h1>
      <p class="info-lead">For Android satellite app data in the US, this catalog currently covers T-Mobile T-Satellite with Starlink. You need a compatible phone, a qualifying plan, and an app that T-Mobile currently supports.</p>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href={tMobileEligibilityUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check whether your phone works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="options-heading">
      <div class="info-section-heading">
        <h2 id="options-heading">T-Satellite service options</h2>
        <p>Choose based on your current mobile service. Prices and information about included plans were checked {checkedDate} and can change.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-paths">
        <section>
          <div>
            <p class="section-eyebrow">Existing T-Mobile customer</p>
            <h3>Check whether your plan includes T-Satellite</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>T-Satellite is included at no extra cost with eligible plans. T-Mobile's current service page names Experience Beyond 2.0 and Better Value.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={tMobileServiceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check included plans <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section>
          <div>
            <p class="section-eyebrow">Existing T-Mobile customer</p>
            <h3>Add T-Satellite to another plan</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>The add-on is currently $10 per month per line. Eligible customers can add it in T-Life or My T-Mobile under Manage Data &amp; Add-Ons.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={tMobileServiceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View add-on details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section>
          <div>
            <p class="section-eyebrow">Customer of another mobile provider</p>
            <h3>Get T-Satellite without switching providers</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>The service is currently $10 per month per line. Your unlocked phone must support adding and using a T-Mobile eSIM, which is a digital SIM, alongside your existing service.</p>
            <a class="button button-primary" href={tMobileChooseServiceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sign up without switching <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <p class="service-secondary-note">Qualifying non-T-Mobile customers can also <a href={tMobileTrialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">try the T-Mobile network for 30 days</a>. The trial is not an ongoing service plan.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
      <div class="info-section-heading">
        <h2 id="steps-heading">Before using satellite apps</h2>
        <p>Complete these checks while you still have ordinary cellular or Wi-Fi service.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-number">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Check the exact phone</h3>
            <p>Use T-Mobile's checker and enter your phone's IMEI, the identification number found in its settings. Different versions of the same phone model may have different support. Service for non-T-Mobile customers also requires an unlocked phone that supports a digital eSIM.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={tMobileEligibilityUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check whether your phone works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-number">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Activate the service</h3>
            <p>Confirm that T-Satellite is active on the line and that your physical SIM or digital eSIM is set up as T-Mobile requires.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Check and prepare the app</h3>
            <p>T-Mobile's supported-app list and this site's Android app check are separate. Confirm that T-Mobile currently supports the app, then install, update, and sign in before leaving coverage.</p>
            <p>Satellite data is slower and less reliable than ordinary cellular data. Features may take longer or be unavailable, even in a supported app.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={tMobileAppsUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check T-Mobile's app list <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="emergency-heading">
      <div class="info-section-heading">
        <h2 id="emergency-heading">Emergency satellite features are different</h2>
        <p>T-Mobile Text to 911, Apple Emergency SOS, and Pixel Satellite SOS provide emergency communication on eligible phones. They are not service plans for running the Android apps in this catalog over satellite.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="source-links">
        <a href={tMobileText911Url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">T-Mobile Text to 911 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={appleSatelliteUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apple Emergency SOS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={pixelSatelliteUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pixel Satellite SOS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Sources checked {checkedDate}</p>
      <h2 id="sources-heading">Current T-Mobile information</h2>
      <p class="info-copy">Pricing, included plans, supported phones, and satellite features can change. T-Mobile's checker and service pages give the final answer for your phone and account.</p>
      <div class="source-links">
        <a href={tMobileServiceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">T-Satellite service <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={tMobileChooseServiceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sign up without switching providers <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={tMobileEligibilityUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check a phone by IMEI <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={tMobileSupportUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">T-Satellite support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
